Parameter data used by the core packages is drawn from published sources with no redistribution
restrictions. Values are transcribed with citations recorded in docs/sources/bibliography.md:

  - de Leva, P. (1996). Adjustments to Zatsiorsky-Seluyanov's segment inertia parameters.
    Journal of Biomechanics 29(9), 1223-1230.
  - Gordon, C. C., et al. (2014). 2012 Anthropometric Survey of U.S. Army Personnel (ANSUR II).
    US Army Natick Soldier RD&E Center. US federal government work.
  - Wu, G., et al. (2002, 2005). ISB recommendations on joint coordinate system definitions.
    Journal of Biomechanics 35(4) and 38(5).
  - Rajagopal, A., et al. (2016). Full-body musculoskeletal model for muscle-driven simulation of
    human gait. IEEE TBME 63(10), 2068-2079. Model freely distributed via SimTK.

Reference models, vendored under tools/validate-external/ for the validation of spec section
13.6 and not compiled into any package:

  - MyoSuite myo_sim (MyoHub) - Apache-2.0, with its licence alongside it. Pinned to a commit;
    see that directory for the pin and how to verify it.

Third-party software dependencies:

  - Rapier (dimforge) - Apache-2.0
  - MuJoCo (Google DeepMind) - Apache-2.0
  - three.js - MIT

Skeleton data -- bone geometry, placement, landmarks, joint centres, and everything derived from
them in packages/skeleton and packages/assets-anatomical -- is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and derives
from:

  - Z-Anatomy (z-anatomy.com, github.com/Z-Anatomy) - CC BY-SA 4.0
  - BodyParts3D, Database Center for Life Science, Japan - CC BY-SA 2.1 JP

Code packages remain Apache-2.0: they are not derivatives of the data they load. See ADR-009 and
ADR-011. No non-commercially-licensed material enters distributed data, because a non-commercial
licence cannot be combined with CC BY-SA in one work.
